# 🚀 CI/CD Pipeline: Jenkins + Docker + Kubernetes (EKS) on AWS

This project demonstrates a production-style CI/CD pipeline for a Java Maven application using Jenkins, Docker, Amazon ECR, and Kubernetes on AWS EKS.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

GitHub → Jenkins → Maven Build → Docker Image → Amazon ECR → Kubernetes (EKS)

---

## 🧰 Tech Stack

- Java (Maven)
- Jenkins (CI/CD)
- Docker
- AWS ECR
- Kubernetes (EKS)
- GitHub

---

## ⚙️ Pipeline Flow

1. Checkout code from GitHub  
2. Increment application version automatically  
3. Build Java application using Maven  
4. Build Docker image  
5. Push image to Amazon ECR  
6. Deploy to Kubernetes (EKS)  
7. Update deployment using rolling updates  
8. Commit version bump back to GitHub  

---

## ☸️ Kubernetes

- Deployment with 2 replicas  
- Service exposed via LoadBalancer  
- Rolling updates enabled  

---

## 🔐 Credentials Used

- AWS Access Key + Secret Key  
- GitHub Personal Access Token  
- Jenkins credentials store  

---

## 🚀 How to Run

1. Setup Jenkins with Docker, Maven, AWS CLI, kubectl  
2. Configure AWS EKS cluster (`demo-cluster`)  
3. Add Jenkins credentials  
4. Run pipeline from Jenkins  
5. Application deploys automatically to Kubernetes  

---

## 📌 Status

✔ CI/CD pipeline completed  
✔ Automated deployment to AWS EKS  
✔ Docker image pushed to Amazon ECR  